  "description": "Faithful replication of the street-tree survey of Kim, Lee, Lee & Choi (2021), Citizens' Preference and Perception of Street Trees of Main Boulevards in Busan, South Korea, Sustainability 13(6): 3141. Participants see street photographs of the 12 most common street tree species in Busan and (1) rate each on 15 five-point word pairs (6 visual properties, 9 affective properties), (2) pick their three most and three least preferred species and say why, (3) rate the similarity of every pair of species (66 pairs), then give gender, age, education, monthly income and years of residence. Property ratings are keyed by species; similarity by species pair.",
